## Composition with body links

When a memorial body contains a markdown link `[text](target.md)`, the codec extracts it as a `:mm/Link` entity.  Promoting that to a `mentions:` typed-edge in frontmatter makes the relation queryable + survives body refactoring.

## Formal ontology mappings

Aligned predicates from established formal vocabularies:

- **CiTO** `cito:mentions` — exact semantic match (passing-reference predicate)
- **PROV-O** `prov:wasInformedBy` — distant analogue (informational influence, broader scope)
- **DC Terms** — no direct equivalent
- **PAV** — no direct equivalent
- **OWL / RDFS** — no direct equivalent

